course: dictionary
lesson: 14763
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word prospect has more than one meaning, so the words around it tell you which one is right. Look for clues in the sentence, then try your meaning in place of the word to check it.
explain: «There is little prospect of rain today.» Here prospect means a possibility, a chance that something will happen. Little prospect means rain is not very likely.
explain: «She has good prospects in her job.» Here prospects means chances of success in the future. Swap in the word chances and the sentence still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Prospect can also be a doing word. «The miners went to prospect for gold in the hills.» Here prospect means to search land for gold, oil or minerals. The words for gold and in the hills are the clues.
fact: Prospect can be a noun (a prospect, prospects) or a verb (to prospect).
fact: «The prospect of a holiday» means an event you expect, something you look forward to.
fact: «Prospects» in the plural means chances of success in the future, especially in a job, as in «job prospects».
fact: Gold prospectors searched for gold in places such as California, Australia and the Yukon.
fact: In literary writing, a prospect can also mean a wide view of land, such as a view from a hill.
exercise: «There is little prospect of rain today.» What does prospect mean here? | A mistake in a sum | *A chance that something will happen | A gold mine | A wide view of land
exercise: Tom is a bright young prospect in the football team. What does prospect mean here? | A football boot | A place where the team trains | A rule about passing the ball | *A player likely to do well in the future
exercise: «The miners went to prospect for gold in the hills.» What does prospect mean here? | To count money in a bank | To paint a picture of the hills | *To search land for gold | To sleep in a tent
test: «She has good prospects in her job.» What do prospects mean here? | *Chances of success in the future | A wide view of the hills | Lots of rain | Money saved in the bank
test: «The prospect of a day at the beach made Sam smile.» What does prospect mean here? | A view of the sea from a cliff | To search the sand for gold | *An event you expect and look forward to | A kind of beach towel
exam: «From the top of the hill we had a wide prospect of the valley.» What does prospect mean here? | *A wide view of land | A possibility of rain | A kind of hill | To search land for gold
